        "id": 20053,
        "name": "drkrash1969",
        "username": "drkrash1969",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/eada6e/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2020-07-18T15:07:59.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I want to put the heroes up against a nano-creature similar to the monster in the Big Hero 6 movie.&nbsp; I thought this might be better served as an Environment rather than a Villain or just a Challenge.</p>\n<p>I'm finding the process to make an Environment to be the most GM-time-intensive thing I've had to do with this system so far.</p>\n<p>Three questions:</p>\n<p>1) In your opinion, does an Environment seem the right way to go for an encounter like this?</p>\n<p>2) Any ideas for Twists?</p>\n<p>3) In earlier stories, the heroes stopped the Big Bad from getting what he needed to make this monster perfect.&nbsp; Should I reflect that in making Twists more \"neutral,\" i.e. have some that affect everyone or even help the heroes? And/or should I make Challenges that could \"end\" the Environment (i.e, end the scene)? Or maybe just Challenges to roll back the Scene Tracker to keep the creature from getting full-powered (i.e., Red Zone)?</p>\n<p>Any brainstorms would be much appreciated.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:53:59.613Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
