        "raw": "<p>I want to put the heroes up against a nano-creature similar to the monster in the Big Hero 6 movie.&nbsp; I thought this might be better served as an Environment rather than a Villain or just a Challenge.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I'm finding the process to make an Environment to be the most GM-time-intensive thing I've had to do with this system so far.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Three questions:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>1) In your opinion, does an Environment seem the right way to go for an encounter like this?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>2) Any ideas for Twists?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>3) In earlier stories, the heroes stopped the Big Bad from getting what he needed to make this monster perfect.&nbsp; Should I reflect that in making Twists more \"neutral,\" i.e. have some that affect everyone or even help the heroes? And/or should I make Challenges that could \"end\" the Environment (i.e, end the scene)? Or maybe just Challenges to roll back the Scene Tracker to keep the creature from getting full-powered (i.e., Red Zone)?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Any brainstorms would be much appreciated.</p>",
