      {
        "id": 231693,
        "name": "Sonvar",
        "username": "Powerhound_2000",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/{size}/1859_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-07-18T15:36:50.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>1. &nbsp;Feels more like you should have a Villain&nbsp;still with just a more hostile environment&nbsp;or at least one that aids the villain&nbsp;</p>\n<p>2. &nbsp;Hinders of various types seem appropriate with dealing with loads of tiny creatures for the heroes. &nbsp; Boosts to the villain by the nanites&nbsp;enhancing them</p>\n<p>3. &nbsp;There's lots of way I could see doing that. &nbsp; Maybe the villain come come in with permanent hinder to represent imperfection. &nbsp; The heroes have some exclusive boost to show they have an advantage. &nbsp;The villain takes a few turns to engage in the fight as they are still being awoken. &nbsp;A Challenge you have planned might require one less box to complete.&nbsp;</p>",
